            "tag_3": "Traditions",
            "caption": "Rituals",
            "heading": "The Season of Moongodi",
            "description": "<p>In the winters of Marwar, the kitchen no longer remained downstairs. It climbed to the terrace. The bedsheets were stretched neatly across the floor, their corners held down by brass lottas so the winter breeze would not disturb them. A heavy steel paraat rested in the warmest patch of sunlight, filled with pale urad batter that had been soaking since the previous evening. Someone tested the batter with a spoon, watched it fall back into the bowl, nodded quietly, and began placing the first wadi onto the cloth.</p>",
            "cta_text": "Read More",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/rituals/the-season-of-moongodi"
          }
