            "tag_3": "Traditions",
            "caption": "Rituals",
            "heading": "The Hour Between",
            "description": "<p>When Business Learnt to Pause</p><p>Across the business communities of western India, there is an hour that has quietly survived every generation. It is neither part of the workday nor entirely home. It begins somewhere between the closing of a ledger and the first handful of namkeen. A pause where conversations have long carried far more than business.</p>",
            "cta_text": "Read More",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/rituals/the-hour-between"
          }
        },
        "slide_7xGQwy": {
